From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Leung <untilscour@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:45:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix wcid->pktid corruption in
 mt76_wcid_cleanup()

mt76_wcid_cleanup() releases dev->status_lock before calling
idr_destroy(&wcid->pktid) to tear down the pktid idr. Meanwhile,
mt76_tx_status_skb_add() can concurrently insert into that same idr
during TX completion handling.

Run idr_destroy() while status_lock is still held so teardown and
concurrent insertion are mutually exclusive.

Closes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/24594
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260820-mt76-pktid-idr-race-v1-1-451f176a6495@protonmail.com
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24810
Signed-off-by: Ryan Leung <untilscour@protonmail.com>
---
 mac80211.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1760,9 +1760,12 @@ void mt76_wcid_cleanup(struct mt76_dev *
 
 	mt76_tx_status_lock(dev, &list);
 	mt76_tx_status_skb_get(dev, wcid, -1, &list);
-	mt76_tx_status_unlock(dev, &list);
-
+	/*
+	 * Serialize pktid teardown against mt76_tx_status_skb_add(), which
+	 * allocates entries in the same idr under status_lock.
+	 */
 	idr_destroy(&wcid->pktid);
+	mt76_tx_status_unlock(dev, &list);
 
 	/* Remove from sta_poll_list to prevent list corruption after reset.
 	 * Without this, mt76_reset_device() reinitializes sta_poll_list but
